            <ArticleTitle>Late cardiac perforation after transcatheter closure of patent foramen ovale.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e29-30</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Cardiac perforation after transcatheter closure of a patent foramen ovale is a very rare complication. We report a case of left atrial wall perforation and aortic root erosion occurring 16 months after implantation of an Amplatzer patent foramen ovale occluder that required emergent surgery.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
